{"id":"iddo","name":"Iddo","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:iddo"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Iddo","text":"(1.) Timely (1 Chr. 6:21). A Gershonite Levite. (2.) Lovely. The son of Zechariah (1 Chr. 27:21), the ruler of Manasseh in David’s time. (3.) Timely. The father of Ahinadab, who was one of Solomon’s purveyors (1 Kings 4:14). (4.) Lovely. A prophet of Judah who wrote the history of Rehoboam and Abijah (2 Chr. 12:15). He has been identified with Oded (2 Chr. 15:1). (5.) Lovely. The father of Berachiah, and grandfather of the prophet Zechariah (Zech. 1:1, 7). He returned from Babylon (Neh. 12:4)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5714","lemma":"עִדּוֹ","xlit":"ʻIddôw","gloss":"Iddo , the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Iddo","count":10,"share":0.77},{"strong":"H2148","lemma":"זְכַרְיָה","xlit":"Zᵉkaryâh","gloss":"Zecarjah, the name of twenty-nine Israelites","kjv":"Zachariah, Zechariah","count":6,"share":0.46},{"strong":"H5030","lemma":"נָבִיא","xlit":"nâbîyʼ","gloss":"a prophet or inspired man","kjv":"prophecy, that prophesy, prophet","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H5029","lemma":"נְבִיא","xlit":"nᵉbîyʼ","gloss":"a prophet","kjv":"prophet","count":2,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1599","lemma":"גִּנְּתוֹן","xlit":"Ginnᵉthôwn","gloss":"Ginnethon or Ginnetho, an Israelite","kjv":"Ginnetho, Ginnethon","count":2,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1247","lemma":"בַּר","xlit":"bar","gloss":"a son, grandson, etc.","kjv":"old, son","count":2,"share":0.15}],"verses":["1Kgs.4.14","1Chr.6.21","2Chr.12.15","2Chr.13.22","Ezra.5.1","Ezra.6.14","Neh.12.4","Neh.12.16","Zech.1.1","Zech.1.7","1Chr.27.21","2Chr.9.29","Ezra.8.17"],"related":[{"id":"zechariah-zecharias","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.115,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"barachiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H5714","why":"both lead with עִדּוֹ (H5714)"},{"id":"ginnethon","type":"lexical","strong":"H5714","why":"both lead with עִדּוֹ (H5714)"},{"id":"jehiel","type":